   "subject": "Re: Proxy authentication error while setAccountInfo()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Problem solved - I used the following options combination, leaving out the domain information in the user name, which allowed me to tunnel through.<div><br></div><div><pre style=\"padding:9.5px;font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;color:rgb(51,51,51);border-radius:4px;line-height:20px;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.14902);background:rgb(247,247,247)\"><code style=\"font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;color:inherit;border-radius:3px;background-color:transparent\">options<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">(</span>RCurlOptions <span style=\"color:rgb(166,127,89);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.498039)\">=</span> list<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">(</span>proxy <span style=\"color:rgb(166,127,89);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.498039)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,153,0)\">&quot;PROXY:PORT&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">,</span> proxyuserpwd<span style=\"color:rgb(166,127,89);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.498039)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,153,0)\">&quot;USER:PWD&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">,</span> verbose <span style=\"color:rgb(166,127,89);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.498039)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(153,0,85)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">)</span></code></pre></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
